#
# Worked projection scene for the two documentation-maturity GATE queries. It
# mirrors the shape crates/docs projects into the graph/documentation named graph:
# a gmeow:DocumentedSlice record gmeow:documents the real slice IRI and carries the
# per-slice gmeow:docCoversDimension incidence, while the CLAIMED tier
# (gmeow:sliceDocMaturity) is asserted on the real slice IRI (its manifest), so the
# gate query bridges record → slice via gmeow:documents exactly as it must over the
# regenerated bundle. Lives under tests/ (NOT examples/) on purpose: it is gate
# test-data only and must NOT enter the docs projection universe.
#
# Two records are demonstrated:
#   1. A SUPPORTED slice — asserts gmeow:docMaturityMinimal and covers that anchor's
#      whole intent (gmeow:dimDefinition, gmeow:dimLabel), so maturity-not-supported.rq
#      returns EMPTY (the headline gate holds).
#   2. An UNDER-DOCUMENTED grounding-slice term — owned by the logic grounding slice
#      and MISSING the three grounding-tier dimensions, so grounding-gaps.rq returns
#      it (the burn-down that drives the grounding lift).

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/documentation/tests/> .

# --- 1. A slice that CLAIMS a tier and EARNS it (gate holds → empty). ------------
# The documentation record carries the covered-dimension incidence; the claim is
# asserted on the real slice IRI, bridged by gmeow:documents.
ex:recordSliceSupported a gmeow:DocumentedSlice ;
    rdfs:label            "Documentation entry: slice supported"@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:documents       ex:sliceSupported ;
    gmeow:docCoversDimension gmeow:dimDefinition , gmeow:dimLabel ;
    gmeow:docEarnedMaturity  gmeow:docMaturityMinimal ;
    gmeow:coverageFraction   "1.0"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#decimal> .

ex:sliceSupported
    rdfs:label            "A slice claiming the minimal maturity it earns"@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:sliceDocMaturity gmeow:docMaturityMinimal .

# --- 2. A grounding-slice term missing its grounding-tier dimensions. ------------
# Owned by the logic grounding slice and missing the fixture pair, worked instance,
# and competency rationale — the exact gaps the grounding lift closes.
ex:recordGroundingGap a gmeow:DocumentedTerm ;
    rdfs:label            "Documentation entry: an under-documented logic term"@x-gmeow-english ;
    gmeow:documents       ex:logicTermUnderDocumented ;
    gmeow:docOwnerSlice   <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/slices/logic> ;
    gmeow:docMissesDimension
        gmeow:dimFixturePair ,
        gmeow:dimWorkedInstance ,
        gmeow:dimCompetencyRationale .
